SCOPE OF THIS LICENSE

The MIT grant above covers the CODE and the stored result files only. Two other
components of this repository carry different terms.

1. The ANNOTATION -- the four independent labels, the final label and the
   annotation rubric in `dados/corpus-rubrica.md` -- is the authors' own work
   and is released under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
   license (CC BY 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.

2. The TRANSCRIBED SENTENCES in `dados/corpus.csv`, and the titles,
   descriptions and sentences in `dados/reordenacao_buscas.csv`, are
   transcribed or copied from public YouTube videos owned by third parties.
   They are reproduced as quotation, only to the extent needed to verify the
   results reported in the paper. Neither the MIT grant nor the CC BY grant
   extends to that material: the rights remain with the respective owners, and
   the source link accompanies every row so provenance can be checked. No
   video, audio or subtitle file is redistributed.

The SentiLex-PT lexicon used as a baseline is a third-party resource under its
own terms and is not redistributed here -- see experimentos/README.md for where
to obtain it.
